meta {
  name: Paths list
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{relayApi}}/v3/paths/list
  body: none
  auth: none
}

tests {
  test("answers one item per path the relay carries", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
    expect(res.body.items).to.be.an("array");
  });
}

docs {
  # Paths list

  Every path the relay carries, with its tracks, its `bytesReceived` counter and its readers.

  This is the one call the app's watch poll always makes, and the rest of a fetch follows from it.
  A reader here is a type and an id, and the type decides which per-protocol list describes it.

  Tracks name coding formats, in either the ITU or the MPEG spelling depending on how the stream was ingested.
  `backend/internal/relay` maps both onto the bitstream format the codec table keys on, and a path whose tracks name no format this app knows is carried in the snapshot as a stream with no format rather than dropped.

  Path names are group-prefixed where the deployment has groups, so a path reads as `<group id>/<stream name>`.
}
